                        "review": "2D Space Minecraft. Seriously. You start out with a simple trusty mining laser and a newbie station, build further crafting systems, build ships, build more SPACE STATIONS, and so on.\n\nI've always had trouble telling from the trailers of these sorts of games whether they emphasize the arcade/shooting parts, or maybe they're FTL clones, or just really boring and cheaply made. But this is the real deal so far, for me.\n\nGraphics that don't look like some poorly put-together Unity thing. Instead you have pretty block-graphics, lighting effects, and a very snappy responsive interface.\n\nAlso there are actual PHASER ARCS like star trek that you have to aim, which should give an idea of the kind of game you're getting into.\n\nWish there were quests and other star systems to visit, but comparable things are already in the feature list and will be coming soon enough if the devs are to be trusted. Based on what I've seen, I believe in them.\n\nP.S. A server browser would be really nice and would encourage early adopters to get together easier, I think.",
